  ('ECO 476', 'Project Appraisal II', 'University of Nigeria, Nsukka', 'Faculty of Social Sciences', 'Economics', '400 Level', 'second', 2, 'The project and overall view of economic development programming; Identification and selection of projects; Project analysis: technical analysis, economic analysis, financial analysis, institutional analysis, social benefit-cost analysis, valuation and shadow prices; Cost-effectiveness analysis; Impact analysis; Reporting; Monitoring and ex-post evaluation; Case studies.', '["The project and overall view of economic development programming", "Identification and selection of projects", "Project analysis: technical analysis, economic analysis, financial analysis, institutional analysis, social benefit-cost analysis, valuation and shadow prices", "Cost-effectiveness analysis; Impact analysis", "Reporting; Monitoring and ex-post evaluation", "Case studies"]'::jsonb, 'Department of Economics handbook'),
  ('ECO 478', 'Project Report', 'University of Nigeria, Nsukka', 'Faculty of Social Sciences', 'Economics', '400 Level', 'second', 6, 'Under the supervision of an academic staff, a student is expected to present a project/research report on any economic issue. The student is expected to display a firm grasp of economic theory being investigated with good mastery of research methodology and econometrics.', '["Under the supervision of an academic staff, a student is expected to present a project/research report on any economic issue", "The student is expected to display a firm grasp of economic theory being investigated with good mastery of research methodology and econometrics"]'::jsonb, 'Department of Economics handbook'),
  ('ECO 428', 'Advanced Monetary Economics', 'University of Nigeria, Nsukka', 'Faculty of Social Sciences', 'Economics', '400 Level', 'second', 2, 'Demand for Money Theories: Quantity theory, Keynesian liquidity theory, Friedman''s modern quantity theory; Determinants of money supply; Theory of inflation; Monetary policy transmission mechanisms; Financial structure and market problems; asymmetric information, adverse selection, moral hazards, and transaction costs; Banking industry and competition; General principles of bank liquidity management, liability management, asset management, capital adequacy; Money management, liquidity management, international monetary and financial system: Bretton Woods system; Different exchange rate regimes; Role and operations with reference to LDCs.', '["Demand for Money Theories: Quantity theory, Keynesian liquidity theory, Friedman''s modern quantity theory", "Determinants of money supply; Theory of inflation", "Monetary policy transmission mechanisms", "Financial structure and market problems; asymmetric information, adverse selection, moral hazards, and transaction costs", "Banking industry and competition", "General principles of bank liquidity management, liability management, asset management, capital adequacy", "International monetary and financial system: Bretton Woods system; Different exchange rate regimes; Role and operations with reference to LDCs"]'::jsonb, 'Department of Economics handbook'),
  ('ECO 453', 'Advanced Demography and Population Economics', 'University of Nigeria, Nsukka', 'Faculty of Social Sciences', 'Economics', '400 Level', 'second', 2, 'Vital rates and ratios; Techniques of population projection: interpolation and graduation in demographic analysis, population change and economic growth; Demographic transition during the process of development; Income; Mortality; Fertility choices and human capital accumulation nexus; Demography of labour force; Analysis of labour force participation; Unemployment, Economic dependency; Occupational segregation (by age, gender etc); Labour market transitions.', '["Vital rates and ratios", "Techniques of population projection: interpolation and graduation in demographic analysis, population change and economic growth", "Demographic transition during the process of development", "Income; Mortality; Fertility choices and human capital accumulation nexus", "Demography of labour force; Analysis of labour force participation", "Unemployment, Economic dependency; Occupational segregation (by age, gender etc)", "Labour market transitions"]'::jsonb, 'Department of Economics handbook'),
  ('ECO 464', 'Health Economics and Health Policy', 'University of Nigeria, Nsukka', 'Faculty of Social Sciences', 'Economics', '400 Level', 'second', 2, 'Further treatment of healthcare demand and supply/production; Efficiency in healthcare provision; Market failure in health care provision; Healthcare financing and universal coverage (including analysis of equity in health care financing, financing and benefit incidence analysis, etc); Economic effects of health care expenditures in developing countries and coping mechanisms; Health systems; Social determinants of health; Costing in economic evaluation; Measuring effectiveness, Outcome measurement, Cost effectiveness/utility analysis; Role of economic evaluation in health care; Term paper.', '["Further treatment of healthcare demand and supply/production; Efficiency in healthcare provision", "Market failure in health care provision", "Healthcare financing and universal coverage (including analysis of equity in health care financing, financing and benefit incidence analysis, etc)", "Economic effects of health care expenditures in developing countries and coping mechanisms", "Health systems; Social determinants of health", "Costing in economic evaluation; Measuring effectiveness, Outcome measurement, Cost effectiveness/utility analysis", "Role of economic evaluation in health care", "Term paper"]'::jsonb, 'Department of Economics handbook'),
  ('ECO 466', 'Climate and Environmental Economics', 'University of Nigeria, Nsukka', 'Faculty of Social Sciences', 'Economics', '400 Level', 'second', 2, 'The Economics of climate change: indicators of climate change and impact of climate change on agriculture, aquatic life, deforestation, tourism, flooding, water availability, carbon cycling and greenhouse effect, environment and health; Concepts of Value: the assets of nature, and economic concept of value, classifications of value; Valuing environmental goods: cost-benefit analysis (CBA), contingent valuation method (CVM), hedonic pricing (HP) method and travel cost method (TCM); Applications of the techniques to environmental damage and benefits such as economic valuation, total economic value (calculations); Pollution abatement benefits in developing countries: The concept of sustainable development (SD); Global Summits on SD; Indicators of sustainable development; Divergent views on sustainable development; The role of public-private partnerships in ensuring best practices; The relationship between SD indicators and MDGs beyond 2015; Concept of intergenerational equity; Intergenerational compensation; Sustainable development and environmental capital.', '["The Economics of climate change: indicators of climate change and impact of climate change on agriculture, aquatic life, deforestation, tourism, flooding, water availability, carbon cycling and greenhouse effect, environment and health", "Concepts of Value: the assets of nature, economic concept of value, classifications of value", "Valuing environmental goods: cost-benefit analysis (CBA), contingent valuation method (CVM), hedonic pricing (HP) method and travel cost method (TCM)", "Applications of the techniques to environmental damage and benefits such as economic valuation, total economic value (calculations)", "Pollution abatement benefits in developing countries: The concept of sustainable development (SD); Global Summits on SD; Indicators of sustainable development", "Divergent views on sustainable development; The role of public-private partnerships in ensuring best practices", "The relationship between SD indicators and MDGs beyond 2015; Concept of intergenerational equity; Intergenerational compensation", "Sustainable development and environmental capital"]'::jsonb, 'Department of Economics handbook'),
  ('ECO 471', 'Industrial Relations and Personnel Management', 'University of Nigeria, Nsukka', 'Faculty of Social Sciences', 'Economics', '400 Level', 'second', 2, 'The concept of industrial relations; Theories of industrial relations; Trade unions: government and structure; Central labour organization and international affiliations; The ILO, Union solidarity and check-off systems; Collective bargaining, industrial conflict and dispute settlement with case studies; Dispute settlements through mediation, arbitration and joint consultation; The state and industrial relations; Comparative industrial relations; Personnel management: recruitment, selection, employee maintenance, training and career development, safety, health, employee services, compensation administration, performance appraisal; Industrial Relations in Nigeria.', '["The concept of industrial relations; Theories of industrial relations", "Trade unions: government and structure; Central labour organization and international affiliations; The ILO, Union solidarity and check-off systems", "Collective bargaining, industrial conflict and dispute settlement with case studies", "Dispute settlements through mediation, arbitration and joint consultation", "The state and industrial relations; Comparative industrial relations", "Personnel management: recruitment, selection, employee maintenance, training and career development, safety, health, employee services, compensation administration, performance appraisal", "Industrial Relations in Nigeria"]'::jsonb, 'Department of Economics handbook'),
  -- Required ancillary / general studies / elective courses from other departments — real code/title/units from the timetable, description left blank pending a verified source.
  ('COS 101', 'Introduction to Computer I', 'University of Nigeria, Nsukka', 'Faculty of Social Sciences', 'Economics', '100 Level', 'first', 2, 'Concepts of hardware and software; basic subsystems of a digital computer; characteristics of a digital computer; devices/media; types/classes of computer emphasising the PC; history of computers and their generations. Problem-solving: algorithm, flowchart, pseudocode, program/data, running a program. Programming: introduction to Java/BASIC programming language syntax and programming. Booting and shutdown; types of operating system; user interface; managing information, computer malware (virus, etc); computer network; internet and web usage, e-mail, instant messaging, etc. Office applications; use of a statistical package and a database management system.', '["Concepts of hardware and software","basic subsystems of a digital computer","characteristics of a digital computer","devices/media","types/classes of computer emphasising the PC","history of computers and their generations","Problem-solving: algorithm, flowchart, pseudocode, program/data, running a program","Programming: introduction to Java/BASIC programming language syntax and programming","Booting and shutdown","types of operating system","user interface","managing information, computer malware (virus, etc)","computer network","internet and web usage, e-mail, instant messaging, etc","Office applications","use of a statistical package and a database management system"]'::jsonb, 'Department of Computer Science course outline'),
  ('MTH 111', 'Elementary Mathematics I', 'University of Nigeria, Nsukka', 'Faculty of Social Sciences', 'Economics', '100 Level', 'first', 3, 'Elementary Set theory, subsets, union, intersection, complements. Venn diagrams, Real numbers, integers, rational and irrational numbers, mathematical induction, real sequences and series, theory of quadratic equations, binomial theorem. Circular measure, trigonometric functions of angles of any magnitude, addition and factor formulae. Complex numbers, algebra of complex numbers, the Argand Diagram, De Moivre''s theorem, $n$th roots of unity.', '["Elementary Set theory, subsets, union, intersection, complements", "Venn diagrams, Real numbers, integers, rational and irrational numbers, mathematical induction, real sequences and series, theory of quadratic equations, binomial theorem", "Circular measure, trigonometric functions of angles of any magnitude, addition and factor formulae", "Complex numbers, algebra of complex numbers, the Argand Diagram, De Moivre''s theorem, $n$th roots of unity"]'::jsonb, 'Department of Mathematics handbook'),
  ('MTH 121', 'Elementary Mathematics II', 'University of Nigeria, Nsukka', 'Faculty of Social Sciences', 'Economics', '100 Level', 'first', 3, 'Functions of a real variable, graphs, limits and continuity. The derivative as limit of rate of change. Techniques of differentiation. Curve sketching, integration as an inverse of differentiation. Methods of integration, definite integrals. Application of integration to areas and volumes.', '["Functions of a real variable, graphs, limits and continuity", "The derivative as limit of rate of change", "Techniques of differentiation", "Curve sketching, integration as an inverse of differentiation", "Methods of integration, definite integrals", "Application of integration to areas and volumes"]'::jsonb, 'Faculty of Biological Sciences course catalogue'),
  ('GSP 101', 'Use of English I', 'University of Nigeria, Nsukka', 'Faculty of Social Sciences', 'Economics', '100 Level', 'first', 2, 'Man, Society and Language - The Nature, Characteristics and Functions of Language, Human Communication & Language, The English Language and the Nigerian society, World English, Levels and Varieties of English — formal, informal, standard, etc., English in Literature and the Media.

Vocabulary of English - Types, Method of Vocabulary Development, Synonyms, Antonyms, Homonyms, Acronyms, Paronyms, Affixation and other morphological processes, English Language Register, diatypes and dialects.

Listening skill - The listening skill discussed as a receptive and reciprocal activity, Nature, Types, Purposes and Factors that affect Listening, Strategies and Aids for Effective Listening.

Reading Skill - The concept of reading as a linguistic organization and a vehicle of communication. Reading Problems, Levels of Reading, Types of Reading, Causes and Remedies of Reading Failures, Reading Techniques & Strategies (Scanning, Skimming, Phrase reading, Intensive & Extensive reading, Exploiting the topic sentence for main ideas), Reading for details, Reading for evaluation and inference, Reading with questions - SQ3R, PR3, Methods for understanding difficult words in a reading text, Literature reading for study, analysis and comment.

Speaking & Communication Skills - Nature, Process & Development, Principles of Public Speech Making and Social Interaction, The Speech Sounds of English and their Articulation, Phonetic Transcription and Practical Speech Work.

Study Techniques - Choosing study centers and discussion groups, Note-taking during lectures, and from audio-visual equipment, Note-making techniques during private reading and literature search, Summary & Transcoding Techniques, Retrieving information from notes, The dictionary as a study guide.

Basic Research Methods & Term Paper Writing - Research – meaning & nature, Types & Methodology; Data in the Research Process, The Research Report, Process and Techniques, Documentation in Research Reports: Process, Types and Methods, Abbreviations in Research Reports, The term paper as a miniature research report, Practical term paper writing.

Course Evaluation & Grading - Students must attend at least 75% of the lectures to qualify for examination in the course.', '["Man, Society and Language - The Nature, Characteristics and Functions of Language, Human Communication & Language, World English, Levels and Varieties of English", "Vocabulary of English - Types, Method of Vocabulary Development, Synonyms, Antonyms, Homonyms, Acronyms, Paronyms, Affixation and other morphological processes", "Listening skill - Nature, Types, Purposes and Factors that affect Listening, Strategies and Aids for Effective Listening", "Reading Skill - Reading Problems, Levels and Types of Reading, Causes and Remedies of Reading Failures, Reading Techniques & Strategies, Reading for evaluation and inference", "Speaking & Communication Skills - Principles of Public Speech Making and Social Interaction, Phonetic Transcription and Practical Speech Work", "Study Techniques - Note-taking, Note-making, Summary & Transcoding Techniques", "Basic Research Methods & Term Paper Writing - The Research Report, Documentation, Abbreviations, practical term paper writing"]'::jsonb, 'Department of Mechanical Engineering handbook'),
  ('GSP 105', 'Natural Science I', 'University of Nigeria, Nsukka', 'Faculty of Social Sciences', 'Economics', '100 Level', 'first', 2, '', '[]'::jsonb, 'Faculty of Social Sciences course handbook'),
  ('GSP 111', 'Use of the Library and Study Skills', 'University of Nigeria, Nsukka', 'Faculty of Social Sciences', 'Economics', '100 Level', 'first', 2, 'Overview of Library: concepts, history, types and functions. Uses in academic libraries; organization of university library and library users. Library processes and procedures. Acquisition process, Cataloging and classification, LC Scheme, in-House Scheme, DDC. Serials process and circulation processes. Access tools in Library resources: Library catalogues, Indexes, Abstracts, Current contents information in the library. Reference sources: types of reference sources and services. Web resources and online resources. Overview of Databases, Online search strategies for information retrieval. Referencing and citation styles for information reporting. Concept of plagiarism. Learning skills and research skills, ICT skillsets: types of learning and information policies.', '["Overview of Library: concepts, history, types and functions. Uses in academic libraries; organization of university library and library users", "Library processes and procedures. Acquisition process, Cataloging and classification, LC Scheme, in-House Scheme, DDC. Serials process and circulation processes", "Access tools in Library resources: Library catalogues, Indexes, Abstracts, Current contents information", "Reference sources: types of reference sources and services. Web resources and online resources", "Overview of Databases, Online search strategies for information retrieval. Referencing and citation styles for information reporting. Concept of plagiarism", "Learning skills and research skills, ICT skillsets: types of learning and information policies"]'::jsonb, 'Department of Mechanical Engineering handbook'),
  ('PSY 101', 'Introduction to Psychology I', 'University of Nigeria, Nsukka', 'Faculty of Social Sciences', 'Economics', '100 Level', 'first', 2, 'The Science of Psychology: History of Psychology Research methods in Psychology Fields of Psychology and other Disciplines. Biological Basis of Human Development.', '["The Science of Psychology: History of Psychology", "Research methods in Psychology", "Fields of Psychology and other Disciplines", "Biological Basis of Human Development"]'::jsonb, 'Department of Psychology handbook'),
  ('SOC 101', 'Introduction to Sociology I', 'University of Nigeria, Nsukka', 'Faculty of Social Sciences', 'Economics', '100 Level', 'first', 2, '', '[]'::jsonb, 'Faculty of Social Sciences course handbook'),
  ('GEO 101', 'Basic Elements of Landforms and the Hydrosphere', 'University of Nigeria, Nsukka', 'Faculty of Social Sciences', 'Economics', '100 Level', 'first', 2, 'Solar system. The earth in space. Structure and composition of the Earth. Internal structures and processes of the Earth. Classification of rocks. Sedimentary, igneous, metamorphic, Geomorphic cycle. The hydrological cycle and landforms - Endogenic and Exogenic. Erosional cycles. The drainage system and patterns. Coastal landforms. Ocean currents.', '["Solar system. The earth in space. Structure and composition of the Earth", "Internal structures and processes of the Earth", "Classification of rocks: Sedimentary, igneous, metamorphic", "Geomorphic cycle", "The hydrological cycle and landforms - Endogenic and Exogenic. Erosional cycles", "The drainage system and patterns", "Coastal landforms. Ocean currents"]'::jsonb, 'Department of Geography handbook'),
  ('COS 102', 'Introduction to Computer II', 'University of Nigeria, Nsukka', 'Faculty of Social Sciences', 'Economics', '100 Level', 'second', 2, 'Problem solving strategies; concepts and properties of algorithm; role of algorithm in the problem solving process; characteristics of a good algorithm; steps involved in algorithm development. Problem solving strategies: top-down and bottom-up methods; implementation strategies; developing an algorithm for a simple problem; representation of algorithms — flowcharts and pseudocodes; development of flowcharts and pseudocodes, flowchart symbols and uses, program objects. Implementation of algorithms in a programming language such as Visual Basic, Java, C, or C++.', '["Problem solving strategies","concepts and properties of algorithm","role of algorithm in the problem solving process","characteristics of a good algorithm","steps involved in algorithm development","Problem solving strategies: top-down and bottom-up methods","implementation strategies","developing an algorithm for a simple problem","representation of algorithms — flowcharts and pseudocodes","development of flowcharts and pseudocodes, flowchart symbols and uses, program objects","Implementation of algorithms in a programming language such as Visual Basic, Java, C, or C++"]'::jsonb, 'Department of Computer Science course outline'),
  ('MTH 122', 'Elementary Mathematics III', 'University of Nigeria, Nsukka', 'Faculty of Social Sciences', 'Economics', '100 Level', 'second', 3, 'Geometric representation of vectors in 1-3 dimensions, Components, direction cosines. Addition of vectors and multiplication of vectors by a scalar, linear independence. Scalar and vector products of two vectors. Differentiation and integration of vectors with respect to a scalar variable. Two-dimensional coordinate geometry. Straight lines, circles, parabolas, ellipses, hyperbolas. Tangents and normals. Kinematics of a particle. Components of velocity and acceleration of a particle moving in a plane. Force and momentum. Newton''s laws of motion; motion under gravity, projectile motion, resisted vertical motion of a particle, elastic string, motion of a simple pendulum, impulse and impact of momentum. Impact of two smooth elastic spheres. Direct and oblique impacts.', '["Geometric representation of vectors in 1-3 dimensions, Components, direction cosines", "Addition of vectors and multiplication of vectors by a scalar, linear independence", "Scalar and vector products of two vectors", "Differentiation and integration of vectors with respect to a scalar variable", "Two-dimensional coordinate geometry", "Straight lines, circles, parabolas, ellipses, hyperbolas", "Tangents and normals", "Kinematics of a particle", "Components of velocity and acceleration of a particle moving in a plane", "Force and momentum", "Newton''s laws of motion", "Motion under gravity, projectile motion, resisted vertical motion of a particle, elastic string, motion of a simple pendulum, impulse and impact of momentum", "Impact of two smooth elastic spheres", "Direct and oblique impacts"]'::jsonb, 'Department of Mathematics handbook'),
  ('GSP 102', 'Use of English II', 'University of Nigeria, Nsukka', 'Faculty of Social Sciences', 'Economics', '100 Level', 'second', 2, 'Part A: Basic Grammar: Introduction. The concept of grammar and its place in language teaching and learning. Parts of speech and their functions (treated in detail). Closed and open class items in parts of speech, Nominalization, Grammatical Structures: the phrase, the clause and the sentence. Elementary Clause Analysis, Sentence Types, Elements and Patterns. Agreement (Grammatical agreement, Notional agreement, Proximity agreement) Agreement with the correlatives. Direct and Reported Speech, Error typology identification and correction.

Part B: Varieties of writing. Introduction (The Meaning, Nature and Purpose of Writing, Writing Types or Genres and their Characteristics). The paragraph as the basic unit of an essay (Types, Development of the Paragraph, Methods of Paragraph Development, The thesis statement). Point of view and style in writing. Qualities of a good piece of writing: Form, Diction and Content in writing. The Mechanics of Writing: punctuation, spelling and capitalization.

Part C: Writing Genres - Planning and choosing your theme. Deciding your genre. Choosing and developing your plot. Point of view, setting and characterization. Using the language that works. Essay Writing — Narration, Description, Exposition and Argumentation. Technical Writing: Letter Writing, Memorandum Writing, Speech Writing, Agenda and Minutes, own story for practice, Computer-linked writing, types, style, language, and process.', '["Part A: Basic Grammar - The concept of grammar, Parts of speech, Grammatical Structures, Sentence Types, Agreement, Direct and Reported Speech, Error typology", "Part B: Varieties of writing - Meaning, Nature and Purpose of Writing, the paragraph as the basic unit of an essay, the thesis statement, Qualities of a good piece of writing, Mechanics of Writing", "Part C: Writing Genres - Planning and choosing your theme, plot, point of view, setting and characterization", "Essay Writing - Narration, Description, Exposition and Argumentation", "Technical Writing - Letter Writing, Memorandum Writing, Speech Writing, Agenda and Minutes"]'::jsonb, 'Department of Mechanical Engineering handbook'),
  ('GSP 106', 'Natural Science II', 'University of Nigeria, Nsukka', 'Faculty of Social Sciences', 'Economics', '100 Level', 'second', 2, '', '[]'::jsonb, 'Faculty of Social Sciences course handbook'),
  ('STA 132', 'Inference II', 'University of Nigeria, Nsukka', 'Faculty of Social Sciences', 'Economics', '100 Level', 'second', 2, 'Elementary Time Series Analysis. Sampling and Statistical Inference: standard error and sampling distributions of the mean and proportion. Tests of significance for means and proportions. Simple linear regression and correlation.', '["Elementary Time Series Analysis", "Sampling and Statistical Inference: standard error and sampling distributions of the mean and proportion", "Tests of significance for means and proportions", "Simple linear regression and correlation"]'::jsonb, 'Department of Statistics handbook'),
  ('STA 172', 'Laboratory for Inference II', 'University of Nigeria, Nsukka', 'Faculty of Social Sciences', 'Economics', '100 Level', 'second', 2, 'Generation of data using table of random numbers. Presentation and analysis of data. Computations using calculator involving measures of central tendency and dispersion, time series, index numbers, simple linear regression and correlation. Test of significance, one sample only.', '["Generation of data using table of random numbers", "Presentation and analysis of data", "Computations using calculator involving measures of central tendency and dispersion, time series, index numbers, simple linear regression and correlation", "Test of significance, one sample only"]'::jsonb, 'Department of Statistics handbook'),
  ('GEO 102', 'Basic Elements of the Atmosphere and Biosphere', 'University of Nigeria, Nsukka', 'Faculty of Social Sciences', 'Economics', '100 Level', 'second', 2, 'Composition of the atmosphere. Solar radiation. Temperature and atmospheric pressure. The global wind system. Humidity and precipitation. Climates of the continents. Soils: formation, characteristics, development and classification. Distribution of Natural vegetation characteristics, classification and distribution.', '["Composition of the atmosphere. Solar radiation. Temperature and atmospheric pressure", "The global wind system. Humidity and precipitation", "Climates of the continents", "Soils: formation, characteristics, development and classification", "Distribution of Natural vegetation characteristics, classification and distribution"]'::jsonb, 'Department of Geography handbook'),
